# LiH — Ground State Energy via VQE
# ====================================
#
# Lithium hydride, the next step after H₂.
#
# LiH has 4 electrons and 12 spin-orbitals in STO-3G.
# Using a frozen core (Li 1s) and active space of 3 orbitals,
# the Hamiltonian maps to 6 qubits and 62 Pauli terms.
#
# Coefficients generated via OpenFermion/PySCF at equilibrium
# geometry: R(Li-H) = 1.546 Å, STO-3G basis, Jordan-Wigner encoding.
#
# Reference ground state (active space FCI): -7.86418329 Hartree
# Full system FCI:                           -7.88276185 Hartree
# (difference = frozen core approximation error)
#
# This is the same VQE algorithm that ran on H₂ — now on a
# 6-qubit system with 62 Pauli terms. Same syntax. Bigger molecule.

hamiltonian LiH:
    term -7.26361321  identity
    term -0.16041712  pauli_z(q5)
    term -0.16041712  pauli_z(q4)
    term -0.14521130  pauli_z(q3)
